|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ has the opposite direction to $q$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PR}=-2q.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PR} \\\\  & =4p-2q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $r=\\lambda p+\\mu q=4p-2q.$\n\nSince $p∦q,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =4$ and $\\mu =-2$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120277/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120277"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285/selection/263f360b6a1528b3a45ad964b3c30922806ab5d22bf9d2cc9b320ff078bfecc7" :answer/id #uuid "9b15f0ef-62bd-5bf4-b839-6eaeb395f1ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{5}h+\\frac{2}{5}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285/selection/1d5a1027fc12ea44e12095a4814a423460e64c5961fc958f068c3953b3ef7659" :answer/id #uuid "34231eb7-95de-578d-b6fb-bea5404c4896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{2}{5}h+\\frac{3}{5}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285/selection/1a825867fa6d54ad41ccdb71074f8b9f933baa83f5de52d3e91a04e23a3c96f6" :answer/id #uuid "2cfa1f55-551a-5306-bd99-fea04c91ec1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{3}{10}h+\\frac{7}{10}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285/selection/1cb45edf9ceb86c0b143028e011a026bf8baf4dca96143f591c25341bfa69bb5" :answer/id #uuid "3be49e71-5568-5d62-82d7-e93c7a49c9de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{1}{2}h+\\frac{1}{2}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285/selection/2c55ff923b4b558ab0716b0bc5fe2e1159832706c723c4289acdef00cf4c1f2a" :answer/id #uuid "90fd9287-b4a0-5691-951e-3bfea08cd342" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "119c1703-b739-5d7d-ac80-fd52c955b62b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120285/selection/2c55ff923b4b558ab0716b0bc5fe2e1159832706c723c4289acdef00cf4c1f2a" :answer-field/choices ["q-120285/selection/263f360b6a1528b3a45ad964b3c30922806ab5d22bf9d2cc9b320ff078bfecc7" "q-120285/selection/1d5a1027fc12ea44e12095a4814a423460e64c5961fc958f068c3953b3ef7659" "q-120285/selection/1a825867fa6d54ad41ccdb71074f8b9f933baa83f5de52d3e91a04e23a3c96f6" "q-120285/selection/1cb45edf9ceb86c0b143028e011a026bf8baf4dca96143f591c25341bfa69bb5" "q-120285/selection/2c55ff923b4b558ab0716b0bc5fe2e1159832706c723c4289acdef00cf4c1f2a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120285" :question/id #uuid "94886abc-d5f4-549c-88a5-0c9095cd6221" :question/math-academy-id "q-120285" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/c4d26b3db6446f586ca47634d9f9a3a004968a0081b8859ce46b4b4af799d066.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OI}=i$ and $J$ divides $\\overset{―}{HI}$ in the ratio $HJ:JI=3:7.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OJ}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OJ}=\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OH}=h,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OHI,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HI} & =\\overset{\\to }{HO}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{OI} \\\\  & =-h+i \\\\  & =i-h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $HJ:JI=3:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{HJ}=\\frac{3}{10}\\overset{\\to }{HI}=\\frac{3}{10}(i-h).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OJ} & =\\overset{\\to }{OH}+\\overset{\\to }{HJ} \\\\  & =h+\\frac{3}{10}(i-h) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}h+\\frac{3}{10}i.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120285/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120285"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325974/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "2df8c6e0-270d-5147-80a9-af3f7a3e1a71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325974/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d340a3d6-73b6-50ab-9cd4-75007d4de8ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325974/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e73a2f7-1c85-5bd8-8efd-9ce3338efc35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325974/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-325974/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-325974/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325974" :question/id #uuid "d8a903e8-340b-59c1-b98b-e4da25996e2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-325974" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/bae20e625c529ef2157faa4d534a19529c605c9002ed750e56723ff29e265226.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-4b,$ then\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-4b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-4b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-4b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/139a4d4312ecbe42cd3a3859af4f4d7b93f8bbc54548ac5a0244c04e7ba5287b.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-4b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-3a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-4b-3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-4b=-3a-4b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-325974/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-326014"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/de5905301a41f02237a48257a79e457f11ad74186942ca5bcf0002ab041aff91.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $t=\\lambda j+\\mu k$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}\nand \n$\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072133/assets/1be50e101b386f53ea5a2f1474f2e1d2debb8f98380d49a346dda32b37db70f1.png)\n\nIn $△OXT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OX=2|j|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OX}$ has the opposite direction to $j$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OX}=-2j.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $XT=\\frac{1}{2}|k|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{XT}$ has the opposite direction to $k$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-\\frac{1}{2}k.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\nt=\\overset{\\to }{OX}+\\overset{\\to }{XT}=-2j-\\frac{1}{2}k.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda j+\\mu k=-2j-\\frac{1}{2}k.$\n\nSince $k∦j,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
